Z||000000||XDrewX||06-14-2001||11:39 PM||||I am about to aquire a complete 2.8L with auto trans off of a good runnning fiero.....(front end was totaled while parked)...... it engine and trans sitting in cradle.  i am going to rebuild this engine from the ground up.  <BR>My current car has an auto trans, so i am not going to try to switch everyhting to a 5 speed, as i will one day put this engine in my current car.<P>Is there any modifications i could make to the transmission that would give it quicker accelleration and let the engine run at 2000 rpm when driving 65 miles an hour.<P>i have little knowledge about working on the "guts" of a tranny.<BR>  <BR> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||fropuff||06-14-2001||11:43 PM||||4 speed w/ overdrive?  I think that 2000 RPM at 65 is low for our trannys.  Mine's like 3300.  With a 4 speed, it's a lot better.  I'm not sure though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||XDrewX||06-14-2001||11:49 PM||||mine runs about 3500 rpm at 65 mph, but i would LIKE it to run at 2000 rpm, like my 99 grandprix does.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||06-15-2001||12:00 AM||||I was talking to the guy who built the 460 electronic tranny in our Impala SS wagon today (LT1 , Lt4 heads 300+hp) In anycase we got onto the topic of Automatic Fiero's and torque converter selection. A lot of people have the mis conceptiont that the 3800 Tq converter makes there car faster. Of the cars I have heard of that have it , all run slower. They shift harder but thats about it. He susgested a converter out of the 1.8ltr Sunbird , it's looser and works much better with the Fiero's power band , as a pose to the 3800's beefier bottom end. You can over "stall" a car.<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-15-2001||07:20 PM||||TH125 will not do what you want. You will have to change to an AOD transmission to drop cruising RPM anywhere near what you want.||||reg||1
